x86_64-linux  cxx1's element loops `__cxx1_vec_new_1T`, `__cxx1_vec_new_3One`, `__cxx1_vec_del_1T` and its atexit helpers `__cxx1_vec_exit_table`, `__cxx1_vec_exit__ZN1N5innerE`, against clang's `__cxx_global_array_dtor` and `.3` for the same job and its inline construction loops with an `_Unwind_Resume` cleanup should a constructor throw; and the C1/D1 forms of the in-class members. The objects and functions the program declares agree.
x86_64-windows  the same loops against clang's `__cxx_global_array_dtor` pair.
arm64-darwin  the same, under the leading underscore.
